    rdf:value """father. He waited for the train marching up and down dressed in a long Haymarket with almost a bustle, open in front to show a dress suit and gorgeous pins, and on his head was stuck a little straw hat two sizes too small for him!
Sunday April 10.98. Easter Sunday
Horne, Horne, the silent Horne came to lunch. We called at Poggio and found a huge reception [written:  deception ] in full swing and poor Lina looking miserable, and then we had a walk through the woods. Horne stayed to dinner. 
Monday April 11. 1898.
Quiet day of music and dress-making. Mr. Pan called. In the evening we were """^^xsd:string ;
